- Deductible only if you itemize (Schedule A). With only $800 charitable and no other major itemized amounts mentioned, itemizing is unlikely to exceed the HOH standard deduction of $20,800. Keep your receipt for substantiation.

5) Itemize vs standard deduction
- Standard deduction for head of household in 2023 = $20,800. Based on numbers you gave, likely take the standard deduction. Itemize only if your total Schedule A deductions (charitable + state/local taxes up to $10k SALT + mortgage interest + property taxes + other qualifying deductions) exceed $20,800.

