Documentation to keep
- Charitable receipt(s) for the $800 (store the receipt).
- Records for consulting income (invoices, 1099s, bank statements).
- Receipts for any business expenses (the $1,350) and for utilities/rent statements if using actual home‑office method.
- MOHELA 1098‑E (student loan interest paid) and bank 1099‑INTs.

Recommendations / next steps
1. Confirm whether the $1,350 unreimbursed expenses are business (consulting) expenses or employee unreimbursed expenses. If business, claim them on Schedule C.
2. Unless you have other significant itemizable deductions (mortgage interest, big state taxes, medical expenses above threshold, etc.), take the standard deduction.
3. Use the actual home‑office method (Form 8829) for 2023 — it gives a much larger deduction here because of the high rent — provided you have documentation for rent/utilities and the space meets the exclusive/principal-use test.
4. Expect to pay self‑employment tax on the consulting profit (reported on Schedule SE); the home‑office & legitimate business expenses reduce that.
5. Keep all receipts and 1099s/W‑2/1098‑E. If you want, I can draft a checklist of documents to collect.

