- Approx QBI deduction = 20% × $8,763 ≈ $1,753 (this reduces taxable income; use Form 8995 in most simple cases).

Standard deduction vs itemize
- 2023 standard deduction for head of household = $20,800.
- Your listed potential itemized amounts: charitable $800 (with receipt) + maybe state taxes withheld and property/mortgage interest if you have them (you did not list). With only $800 + the amounts above, itemizing will be far below the $20,800 standard deduction.
- Recommendation: take the standard deduction unless you have additional itemizable deductions (state & local tax, mortgage interest, large medical expenses, etc.) exceeding $20,800.

Other tax treatment notes
