- Schedule SE (Self‑Employment Tax) — to calculate SE tax
- Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home) — if you use the regular home‑office method (not needed for simplified)
- Schedule A (Itemized Deductions) — only if you choose to itemize (unlikely based on the amounts you listed)
- Schedule B — only if interest + ordinary dividends exceed $1,500 (your interest total is $1,370 so likely not required)
- Keep Form 1098‑E (student loan interest statement) from MOHELA (you’ll need it if you qualify for the student loan interest deduction), any 1099‑NEC/1099‑MISC for consulting or records of consulting income, and 1099‑INT for bank interest.

Arizona (state) forms
- Arizona Form 140 (Resident Personal Income Tax Return) — attach any state schedules required. Arizona starts with federal AGI so the federal treatment (Schedule C, SE, etc.) flows to the state return. Arizona may allow different adjustments; check the state instructions or let me know if you want help preparing the state return.

4) Documentation to have ready
- W‑2 from Midwest Health Systems
- Any 1099‑NEC / records showing the $15,000 consulting income
- 1099‑INT’s from Citi and Fidelity (or bank statements if no 1099)
