- If the $1,350 are business expenses and your consulting is self‑employment, report the consulting income on Schedule C and claim the home office using the regular allocation (Form 8829) — it looks like the regular method will give you a larger deduction than the simplified method in your situation.
- Take the standard deduction for Head of Household ($20,800) unless you have significantly more itemizable deductions (state tax paid, mortgage interest, major medical, etc.) that weren’t listed here.
- Student loan interest is probably disallowed because your MAGI is likely > $90k; confirm the 2023 interest amount and 1098‑E to be sure.
