4) Home office deduction (you qualify if the space is used regularly and exclusively for business)
You have two methods: simplified vs. actual.

- Simplified method
  - $5 per square foot up to 300 sq ft.
  - For 155 sq ft -> 155 * $5 = $775 deduction (claimed directly on Schedule C; no Form 8829).
  - Easy and often fine for smaller deduction.

- Actual (regular) method
  - Deduct the business share of actual home expenses. Business percentage = home office sq ft / total living area = 155 / 780 ≈ 19.87% (≈0.1987).
